### 1. Register a new user (201)
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sok Sreypov",
  "email": "sreypov@puong.kh",
  "password": "sreypov-pass"
}

### 2. Register the same e-mail again (409)
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Duplicate",
  "email": "sreypov@puong.kh",
  "password": "sreypov-pass"
}

### 3. Invalid body: short name, bad e-mail, short password (400)
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "X",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "short"
}

### 4. Log in as the seeded OWNER (200 { token })
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "theary@puong.kh",
  "password": "theary-password"
}

### 5. Wrong password (401)
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "theary@puong.kh",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### 6. /me without a token (401)
GET http://localhost:3000/me

### 7. /me with the token (200) — paste the token from step 4
GET http://localhost:3000/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. My trees (200)
GET http://localhost:3000/trees
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Create a tree — I become OWNER (201, one transaction)
POST http://localhost:3000/trees
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "The Sok Family",
  "description": "A tree created from requests.http"
}

### 10. Unknown field in the body (400, forbidNonWhitelisted)
POST http://localhost:3000/trees
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Nope",
  "ownerId": 99
}

### 11. Members of tree 1 (200)
GET http://localhost:3000/trees/1/members
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. Invite a member by e-mail (201 / 404 unknown user / 409 already)
POST http://localhost:3000/trees/1/members
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sreypov@puong.kh",
  "role": "CONTRIBUTOR"
}

### 13. Change a member's role (200) — OWNER only
PATCH http://localhost:3000/members/3
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "VIEWER"
}

### 14. Remove a member (204)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/members/3
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 15. Persons of tree 1 (200)
GET http://localhost:3000/trees/1/persons
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 16. Add a person (201) — CONTRIBUTOR required
POST http://localhost:3000/trees/1/persons
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Chanthou Sreyneang",
  "gender": "female",
  "birthDate": "1972-06-14",
  "biography": "Youngest daughter of Sovann and Sophea."
}

### 17. deathDate before birthDate (400)
POST http://localhost:3000/trees/1/persons
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Impossible Dates",
  "birthDate": "1990-01-01",
  "deathDate": "1980-01-01"
}

### 18. Read one person (200 / 404 unknown id)
GET http://localhost:3000/persons/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 19. Edit a person (200)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/persons/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "biography": "Village teacher in Kampong Cham; his diary from 1960 was scanned in 2024."
}

### 20. Delete a person (204 — relationships and memories go with it)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/persons/10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 21. Relationships of tree 1 (200)
GET http://localhost:3000/trees/1/relationships
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 22. Link two persons (201 / 404 person not in this tree / 409 duplicate)
POST http://localhost:3000/trees/1/relationships
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "personId": 1,
  "relatedPersonId": 4,
  "type": "spouse"
}

### 23. A person related to itself (400)
POST http://localhost:3000/trees/1/relationships
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "personId": 1,
  "relatedPersonId": 1,
  "type": "sibling"
}

### 24. Delete a relationship (204)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/relationships/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 25. Memories of a person (200)
GET http://localhost:3000/persons/2/memories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 26. Write a memory (201) — server sets authorId
POST http://localhost:3000/persons/2/memories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "Grandma's amok recipe still refuses to be written down."
}

### 27. Empty content (400)
POST http://localhost:3000/persons/2/memories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": ""
}

### 28. Delete a memory (204 — author or tree OWNER)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/memories/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 29. Someone else's memory, VIEWER tries (403)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/memories/1
Authorization: Bearer {{viewerToken}}

### 30. Non-member reads a tree (403)
GET http://localhost:3000/trees/1
Authorization: Bearer {{outsiderToken}}

### 31. DELETE the tree (204 — persons, memberships, memories all removed)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/trees/9
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
